# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Giscus — GitHub Discussions integration for journal article comments
#
# Setup steps:
#   1. Ensure GitHub Discussions is enabled on your repository.
#   2. Visit https://giscus.app and configure your repository.
#   3. Copy the generated data-repo-id and data-category-id values below.
#   4. Rename this file to .env.local for local development.
#
# All four variables are required for the discussion widget to appear.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

NEXT_PUBLIC_GISCUS_REPO=Shreyas-Agarwal/portfolio-next
NEXT_PUBLIC_GISCUS_REPO_ID=
NEXT_PUBLIC_GISCUS_CATEGORY=Journal Discussion
NEXT_PUBLIC_GISCUS_CATEGORY_ID=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Locked publications — passcode-gated access for publications marked
# "locked": true in their publication.json (e.g. shared with specific people
# rather than published generally). See src/lib/publication/access.ts.
#
# PUBLICATION_LOCK_SECRET signs the access cookie once someone enters the
# right passcode — pick any long random string, it never needs to be shared.
#
# Each locked publication needs its own passcode env var, named
# PUB_PASSCODE_<ID-WITH-DASHES-AS-UNDERSCORES, UPPERCASED>. Example for the
# publication "organizations-run-on-proxies":
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

PUBLICATION_LOCK_SECRET=
PUB_PASSCODE_ORGANIZATIONS_RUN_ON_PROXIES=
PUB_PASSCODE_PHYSICS_OF_INFORMATION_SYSTEMS=
